// Ashspine A: the land, the one source for both the terrain art and the collision mask.
//
// World pixels, y down. Each island is a closed chain of cubic Béziers (two control points, then
// the end), run clockwise on screen: walkable `Top`s left to right, `Rock` for cliffs, plates and
// undersides. Basalt breaks in columns, so cliffs are column faces and keels are stepped column ends.
// Tops are roughened along their normals (`rough` 1.3: basalt breaks jagged) and capped with dry
// grass; rock stays smooth. `dress` places decorations into the map's terrain.svg, one rule per slot
// (`{{name}}`).
//
// A: one massive ridge rising from the abyss, a shelf and a ledge stepping down each flank, and two
// crags a side floating over the drop. High-angle duels over the crest.
